# Witness: an exclusion defined by a row of another table inside section 9

Section 9 may carry more than one table. Only the exclusion table defines: an errata table
whose first cell is an EX- identifier would otherwise launder a citation that nothing in the
bundle actually excludes. The header names the columns, and the header is what decides.

The unmeasured start-up path is recorded as EX-98.

## 9. Exclusions

Corrections to identifiers are carried beside the exclusions themselves.

| ID | Correction |
|---|---|
| EX-98 | The identifier is corrected here rather than renumbered. |

| ID | Status | Exclusion |
|---|---|---|
| EX-01 | Open | The inbound half of the legacy-boundary rule is environment-conditional. |
